From e54af5bcb579ebf384caccfa2e6ded3e38f920ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruslanbay <67730802+ruslanbay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 09:30:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 55/60] media: intel/ipu4: Fix PM runtime reference leak in
 ipu_buttress_authenticate()

Add a missing pm_runtime_put() call for psys_iommu in the exit path of
ipu_buttress_authenticate(). Every authentication attempt (triggered per
video node open) calls pm_runtime_get_sync(&amp;isp->psys_iommu->dev) but failed
to balance it upon completion, leaking a PM reference. This prevented the
PSYS IOMMU from runtime-suspending and blocked subsequent ISYS power island
state transitions after errors.
---
 drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-buttress.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-buttress.c b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-buttress.c
index 84a7f6537..2081d2f5a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-buttress.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-buttress.c
@@ -908,6 +908,13 @@ int ipu_buttress_authenticate(struct ipu_device *isp)
 	dev_info(&isp->pdev->dev, "CSE authenticate_run done\n");
 
 iunit_power_off:
+	/*
+	 * Balance the pm_runtime_get_sync() above: without this every
+	 * authentication (one per video node open) leaks a reference on
+	 * the psys iommu, so neither MMU ever runtime-suspends and the
+	 * isys power island can never be cycled after an error.
+	 */
+	pm_runtime_put(&isp->psys_iommu->dev);
 	mutex_unlock(&b->auth_mutex);
 
 	return rval;
-- 
